title: "frame-system: require explicit weight info in production default configs"

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `frame_system::Config::SystemWeightInfo` and
      `frame_system::Config::ExtensionsWeightInfo` no longer have a default in the
      production presets `SolochainDefaultConfig`, `ParaChainDefaultConfig` and
      `RelayChainDefaultConfig`. Runtimes deriving their `frame_system::Config` from
      one of these presets via `#[derive_impl(...)]` must now set both types
      explicitly:

      ```rust
      #[derive_impl(frame_system::config_preludes::SolochainDefaultConfig)]
      impl frame_system::Config for Runtime {
          // Prefer weights benchmarked for your own runtime over `()`.
          type SystemWeightInfo = ();
          type ExtensionsWeightInfo = ();
          // ...
      }
      ```

      Previously these types silently defaulted to `()`, which resolves to the
      Substrate reference weights benchmarked for a *different* runtime. This is
      almost never correct in production and was an error-prone default (see issue
      #10758).

      `TestDefaultConfig` is intentionally left unchanged: it still defaults both
      weights to `()`, so test mocks deriving from it do not need to be updated.
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `#[register_default_impl]` and `#[derive_impl]` now honour
      `#[pallet::no_default]` when it is placed on an item *inside* a registered
      default impl. Such an item stays part of the default impl (so it remains a
      complete trait implementation) but is no longer copied into impls that derive
      from it, forcing downstream users to set the type explicitly. This already
      matched the documented behaviour of `derive_impl`; it is now actually
      enforced.

